WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.012
Filtering lets us turn a business question into a condition.

00:00:04.012 --> 00:00:09.492
We might ask for orders above a certain amount, orders from a specific channel,

00:00:09.492 --> 00:00:14.007
or records that satisfy several conditions at the same time.

00:00:14.007 --> 00:00:17.532
Pandas uses Boolean masks for this.

00:00:17.532 --> 00:00:24.992
A Boolean mask is simply a sequence of true and false values that tells Pandas which rows to keep.

00:00:24.992 --> 00:00:32.802
When combining conditions, use the ampersand operator for AND and the vertical bar operator for OR,

00:00:32.802 --> 00:00:36.572
with each condition placed inside parentheses.

00:00:36.572 --> 00:00:43.197
Pandas also provides the query method, which can make some filters easier to read.

00:00:43.197 --> 00:00:47.067
The important idea is not the syntax itself.

00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:51.794
It is translating a question into a precise rule for selecting rows.
